  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "source": "/* The Pascal line came out [1/3, −1/9, 1] and the Brianchon point\n   [−1/3, 1/9, 1].  That is not a coincidence — they are pole and polar. */\nBpt  : meet(d1, d2)$\nPline: join(X1, X2)$\nprint(\"Brianchon point         = \", normalise(Bpt))$\nprint(\"its polar w.r.t. the circle = \", normalise(polar(Scirc, Bpt)))$\nprint(\"Pascal line             = \", normalise(Pline))$\nprint(\"same? \", is( normalise(polar(Scirc, Bpt)) = normalise(Pline) ))$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"So polarity in the conic carries the Pascal configuration to the\")$\nprint(\"Brianchon configuration: one theorem, seen twice.\")$",
