  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "source": "/* Picture of the Pascal configuration */\nchart(v) := float([v[1]/v[3], v[2]/v[3]])$\nseg(p,q) := [discrete, [p[1],q[1]], [p[2],q[2]]]$\nmark(ps) := [discrete, map(first, ps), map(second, ps)]$\n\nhx : map(chart, hexa)$\nx1 : chart(X1)$  x2 : chart(X2)$  x3 : chart(X3)$\ncircle_pts : makelist( [cos(2*%pi*k/200), sin(2*%pi*k/200)], k, 0, 200)$\n\nprint(\"hexagon vertices: \", hx)$\nprint(\"Pascal points   : \", [x1, x2, x3])$\n\nplot2d([ [discrete, map(first,float(circle_pts)), map(second,float(circle_pts))],\n         [discrete, append(map(first,hx),[hx[1][1]]),\n                    append(map(second,hx),[hx[1][2]])],\n         seg(hx[1],x1), seg(hx[4],x1),      /* AB and DE meeting at X1 */\n         seg(hx[2],x2), seg(hx[5],x2),      /* BC and EF meeting at X2 */\n         seg(hx[3],x3), seg(hx[6],x3),      /* CD and FA meeting at X3 */\n         seg(x1,x3),                        /* the Pascal line         */\n         mark([x1,x2,x3]) ],\n       [x, -5, 2], [y, -3.5, 3.5],\n       [style, [lines,2],[lines,2],\n               [lines,1],[lines,1],[lines,1],[lines,1],[lines,1],[lines,1],\n               [lines,3],[points,4]],\n       [legend, false], [same_xy, true],\n       [title, \"Pascal: opposite sides of an inscribed hexagon meet on a line\"])$",
